# C9-01 fixture — vendor C: translates B's kind onward, with its own cost.
stratum vendor-c "Vendor C's world, plus its declared translation from B."

use vendor-b as vb

term c "Vendor C's reading kind — the contract's target."
term coarsening "Loss: B's ordinal scale collapses onto C's coarser one."

maps-to vb:b -> c @loss = coarsening
